# Hello from CDN

This page was rendered entirely in the browser - no server-side processing, no build step.

@note
The script tag on the page pulls Markup+ from jsDelivr, then calls MarkupPlus.toHTML() with this source.
@end

## What this proves

- Markup+ works in any modern browser
- No npm, no bundler, no build step
- Just a script tag and a few lines of JavaScript

| Feature | Browser Support |
|---------|:---------------:|
| toHTML | Yes |
| renderBody | Yes |
| renderFragment | Yes |
| Charts | Yes |
| Math | Yes |
| Syntax highlighting | Yes |

@tip
Open DevTools to see the runtime in action.
@end
